From a896d5fed2e3fde3410ce5c2ca643d4e66480c82 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Intel MPSS <mpss@intel.invalid>
Date: Mon, 28 Sep 2026 09:57:36 +0200
Subject: [PATCH 14/16] perf/x86/intel: route KNC (family 11) to the knc PMU
 driver

From Intel MPSS 3.8.6: intel_pmu_init() dispatches family 11 model 1
to knc_pmu_init() (mainline still carries events/intel/knc.c but no
longer reaches it from the family 6 initialisation).

Co-Authored-By: Claude Fable 5.1 <noreply@anthropic.com>
Signed-off-by: Anselm Busse <anselm.busse@outlook.com>
---
 arch/x86/events/intel/core.c | 5 +++++
 1 file changed, 5 insertions(+)

diff --git a/arch/x86/events/intel/core.c b/arch/x86/events/intel/core.c
index fe65be0b9d9c..11bb7b35a15d 100644
--- a/arch/x86/events/intel/core.c
+++ b/arch/x86/events/intel/core.c
@@ -6855,6 +6855,11 @@ __init int intel_pmu_init(void)
 	char *name;
 	struct x86_hybrid_pmu *pmu;
 
+#ifdef CONFIG_MK1OM
+	extern int knc_pmu_init(void);
+	if (boot_cpu_data.x86 == 0x0b)		/* Knights Corner */
+		return knc_pmu_init();
+#endif
 	/* Architectural Perfmon was introduced starting with Core "Yonah" */
 	if (!cpu_has(&boot_cpu_data, X86_FEATURE_ARCH_PERFMON)) {
 		switch (boot_cpu_data.x86) {
